LISS panel microdata
--------------------
The survey data underlying this work come from the LISS panel (Longitudinal
Internet studies for the Social Sciences), administered and managed by the
non-profit research institute Centerdata (Tilburg University, the Netherlands).
Centerdata's user statement prohibits redistribution of LISS data. The raw
files are therefore NOT distributed here and are not ours to license.

Obtain them from the LISS Data Archive (https://www.dataarchive.lissdata.nl/)
after signing the user statement (https://liss.statements.centerdata.nl/);
access is free. The study units used are:

  avars_201102_EN_2.0p    background variables, 2011
  avars_201807_EN_1.0p    background variables, 2018
  avars_201905_EN_1.0p    background variables, 2019
  ed11a_EN_1.0p           Core Study: education, wave a
  oi18a_EN_1.0p           Core Study: income, wave a
  su19a_EN_1.0p           Core Study: social integration, wave a

auxillary/create_hierarchical_agents.py and auxillary/create_pmf_tables.py
rebuild every derived input from these files.

Derived files
-------------
Aggregate tables produced by us from the above (for example the conditional
probability tables in data/demographic_pmfs.pkl) are licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), insofar as the LISS terms
permit their release. Respondent-level derived files are not redistributed.
data/synthetic_agents.csv is a synthetic population sampled from those
aggregate tables by auxillary/create_synthetic_agents.py; it contains no LISS
respondent and is CC BY 4.0 on the same condition.

